HTB Sherlock — Dream Job-2 (Tasks 11–12)
Category	Type	Platform	Date compiled
DFIR / Malware analysis	Sherlock	Hack The Box	March 2026

Skills demonstrated: OOXML document forensics, metadata extraction, static VBA macro analysis with oletools, MITRE ATT&CK mapping.

Scope: this write-up covers Tasks 11 and 12 only. Earlier tasks were threat-intelligence questions answered from open-source research and are summarized under Threat-intelligence context.

Summary

The Sherlock models the Lazarus Group "Operation Dream Job" campaign, which uses fake job offers as phishing lures. Two lure artifacts were analyzed statically on Kali Linux without being executed:

Task 11: the .docx lure's OOXML core properties record Challenger as the last modifier.
Task 12: the 17.dotm macro-enabled template contains a VBA macro that creates the Word startup directory AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Word\STARTUP. Templates placed there load automatically each time Word starts, which provides persistence.
